  "behavior_proved": [
    "TelemetryMetric<T> distinguishes a successful zero from unavailable and stale values while retaining bounded source, reason, capture time, and current observation time.",
    "Available, warming-up, unsupported, temporarily unavailable, and access-denied states are structurally validated, including canonical UTC range and capture-before-observation ordering.",
    "GlobalMemoryStatusEx maps total, available, derived used, and physical-utilization RAM values with exact source identities.",
    "GetPerformanceInfo maps commit pressure, committed bytes, and paged-pool bytes with checked page-to-byte arithmetic and exact source identities.",
    "Active bytes, wired bytes, and swap metrics remain explicitly unsupported rather than being synthesized from semantically different Windows counters.",
    "Compressed bytes remain explicitly unsupported on this qualified machine because typeperf -q \\Memory reported zero exact matches for \\Memory\\Compressed Page Count.",
    "Independent native probe failures preserve successful categories; failed refreshes retain prior values, capture time, and source as stale while recording the current failed observation and reason.",
    "Cancellation and deadline checks bracket every native memory block, overlapping collection is rejected without a queue, and shutdown is idempotent and drains admitted work.",
    "One lifecycle mutex linearizes closed-state checking, admission, active release, publication, and shutdown; deterministic tests bracket pre-admission and post-admission races and reject post-shutdown publication.",
    "The dashboard JSON codec preserves all thirteen legacy RAM keys while adding per-field availability metadata and encoding unavailable values as null.",
    "The new ForgeConductor.Telemetry.Windows layer depends inward on ForgeConductor.Contracts, and the synchronized G04 static graph guardrail accepts that exact dependency edge."
  ],
  "evidence_scope": {
    "proved": "Typed telemetry observation invariants, Windows RAM collection and mapping, stale retention, cancellation/deadline/overlap/shutdown behavior, dashboard RAM JSON compatibility, the current-machine compressed-counter absence, and the telemetry layer boundary in Release x64 on the owner-qualified Windows 11 machine.",
    "not_proved": "CPU, disk, GPU, process-list, network, power, or thermal collection; the P18 producer/mailbox/history lifecycle; production Manager composition replacement; end-to-end live dashboard refresh; resource-budget stress; or the authoritative G17 gate."
  },
